1.0.5 2026-10-30

  - HFS events.tsv: the 6 markers that the authors' analysis file (.ades.mrk) repeats from the acquisition file
    (.mrk), identical in onset, duration and label, are one row each (source = both). The events.tsv files of
    1.0.4 are kept byte for byte in sourcedata/events-v1.0.4/.
  - Both runs, events.tsv: rows decoded from the recorded TRIG channel (source = TRIG). Its lower level is the
    stimulator-on gate: 6 hfs_train rows of 5.05 s (one per 43 Hz train, including the first train at 23.7 s that
    has no marker) and one spes_gate row (11.570-311.532 s, spanning the 20 single pulses). events.json files
    describe the rows (code/fix-20261030/events_dedup_trig.py).
  - coordsystem.json and README: caution that the coordinates are FreeSurfer tkrRAS of a conformed MRI; the
    released T1 is not conformed and its c_ras offset is not released, so the contacts cannot be overlaid on it
    with its affine alone.
  - derivatives/stimartefact (6 files) and code/fix-20261030_stimartefact (6 files): stimulation onsets detected
    from the stimulation artefact (20 SPES pulses, 6 HFS trains), clearly labelled as not from a source; method in
    its README.

1.0.4 2026-10-16
  - dataset_description.json: replaced citation-slug Name with the descriptive title already used in README.

1.0.3 2026-10-07
  - README: corrected the SEEG channel count (128, not 131) and documented the electrode/contact counts from the article,
    its Supplementary Table 1, the released coordinate table and the released recordings.

1.0.2 2026-10-07
  - Metadata from the article full text (Bratu et al. 2021 Cortex): age, sex, handedness, epilepsy onset age, seizure onset,
    SEEG epileptogenic zone, paper electrode/contact counts; recording system (XLTek Quantum, Natus), Dixi electrodes,
    stimulator and stimulation protocol in ieeg.json; Funding verbatim; acknowledgements/disclosure; README.

1.0.1 2026-10-07
  - 2026-10-07 metadata enrichment: participants (diagnosis, lesion, implant type, implanted hemispheres,
    electrode/contact counts, stimulated contacts; age/sex/handedness remain n/a, source silent), participants.json
    levels/descriptions, ieeg.json placement scheme/electrode groups/task descriptions, README restructured,
    dataset_description references/keywords. Sources: article abstract (PubMed 34775265), Dryad record and release files.

